<div>&nbsp;</div>
<h5>Career Outlook</h5>
<hr />
<p>A degree in Communications can open doors to a variety of careers including journalism, law, advertising, public relations, marketing, sales, real estate, and much more. Salary ranges for jobs within these trajectories vary greatly. Public Relations Specialists in California make an average of $56,770 per year according to the <a title="U. S. Department of Labor- Public Relations Specialist" href="http://www.bls.gov/ooh/media-and-communication/public-relations-specialists.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">U.S. Department of Labor</a>.</p>
